{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 26,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In that day shall this song be sung in the land of Judah; We have a strong city; salvation will ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " appoint ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " walls and bulwarks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Open ye the gates, that the righteous nation which keepeth the truth may enter in.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou wilt keep ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in perfect peace, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whose",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mind ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " stayed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "on thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": because he trusteth in thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Trust ye in the LORD for ever: for in the LORD JEHOVAH ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " everlasting strength:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he bringeth down them that dwell on high; the lofty city, he layeth it low; he layeth it low, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the ground; he bringeth it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the dust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The foot shall tread it down, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the feet of the poor, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the steps of the needy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The way of the just ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " uprightness: thou, most upright, dost weigh the path of the just.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, in the way of thy judgments, O LORD, have we waited for thee; the desire of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "our",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " soul ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to thy name, and to the remembrance of thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With my soul have I desired thee in the night; yes, with my spirit within me will I seek thee early: for when thy judgments ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the earth, the inhabitants of the world will learn righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let favor be shown to the wicked, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he will not learn righteousness: in the land of uprightness he will deal unjustly, and will not behold the majesty of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy hand is lifted up, they will not see: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they shall see, and be ashamed for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " envy at the people; yes, the fire of thy enemies shall devour them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "LORD, thou wilt ordain peace for us: for thou also hast wrought all our works in us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD our God, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "other",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lords beside thee have had dominion over us; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by thee only will we make mention of thy name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " dead, they shall not live; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " deceased, they shall not rise: therefore hast thou visited and destroyed them, and made all their memory to perish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast increased the nation, O LORD, thou hast increased the nation; thou art glorified: thou hadst removed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " far to all the ends of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "LORD, in trouble have they visited thee, they poured out a prayer ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy chastening ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As a woman with child, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " draweth near the time of her delivery, is in pain, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " crieth out in her pangs; so have we been in thy sight, O LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have been with child, we have been in pain, we have as it were brought forth wind; we have not wrought any deliverance on the earth; neither have the inhabitants of the world fallen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy dead ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall live, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "together with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust: for thy dew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the dew of herbs, and the earth shall cast out the dead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come, my people, enter thou into thy chambers, and shut thy doors about thee; hide thyself as it were for a little moment until the indignation shall be overpast.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.26.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.26.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For behold, the LORD cometh out of his place to punish the inhabitants of the earth for their iniquity: the earth also shall disclose her blood, and shall no more cover her slain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
